        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 1: interact",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "A question needs a contingent answer. Listen for the person and role being asked about, answer that question, and leave room for the next turn.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "老师",
                "pinyin": "lǎoshī",
                "meaning": "teacher",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "310e6b5e11de6adedbeb20515e73ec6357cf47c84ba79ce43f7858f24ded0eb2"
              },
              {
                "text": "学生",
                "pinyin": "xuéshēng",
                "meaning": "student; schoolchild",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "3a595882d466c8b7a59f2ff0b72dbf61cb896d106d43e5462367c735b4260cbb"
              },
              {
                "text": "您",
                "pinyin": "nín",
                "meaning": "you, used respectfully",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "f16b233bd9075387fbef9b385417347443ced956f316fe0b7a7253d5e84e8a20"
              },
              {
                "text": "你",
                "pinyin": "nǐ",
                "meaning": "you",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "b316ac0dd167bd8bef2048818a93b55be5371efb0af3024556cf9b5c93799d4d"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A teacher asks whether you are a student. In this scene you are a student; the peer next to you has not stated their role. Answer the teacher, then ask the peer whether they are a student and pause for their reply.\nFamiliar meanings available: teacher; student; schoolchild; you, used respectfully; you."
          }
        ]
